# Build-context hygiene for the backend images (context = repo root). The JAR is
# compiled inside the Dockerfile's Maven stage, so no host build outputs should
# enter the context — they'd bloat the upload to the daemon/builder and could
# shadow the freshly built artifact. (The frontend image has its own context,
# frontend/, and is unaffected by this file.)

# Maven / build outputs
**/target/

# Frontend build outputs — not part of the backend reactor, just dead weight here
**/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Local caches that must not leak into an image layer
.m2/
.npm/

# Local env / secrets
.env
*.env

# Editor / OS cruft
.idea/
*.iml
.DS_Store

# NOTE: .git is deliberately NOT ignored. git-commit-id-maven-plugin reads the
# working-copy HEAD during the build to bake the short-SHA into
# META-INF/build-info.properties (VersionController surfaces it as git.sha).
# Excluding .git would silently drop the SHA from the /version endpoint.
